958:% First, we have shown the equivalence of the $k$-Jump rule ($k \geq 3$) and the TJ rule with respect to the reconfigurability. This means that only the $2$-Jump rule can have the reconfigurability power different from both the TJ rule and TS rule. Second, we proposed a polynomial time algorithm solving $2$-\Isreconf\ for split graphs. The existence of this algorithm reveals that the $2$-Jump rule and the TS rule have different power with respect to the reconfigurability.  Finally, we have shown that the \ShortestunderkIsreconf\ is NP-complete. This means that the $k$-Jump rule ($k \geq 3$) and TJ rule have the same power for \Isreconf, but not for \ShortestIsreconf. 
